WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
Take two equal masses
of the same solid.

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.390
Drop the first into
acid as a single lump.

3
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.450
It fizzes gently.

4
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.050
Grind the second into powder
and drop it into the same acid.

5
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.250
It froths over the top.

6
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.830
Now warm the acid, and
it goes faster still.

7
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.030
So what decides how
fast a reaction goes?

8
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.590
In this mission, you'll
measure how fast reactions go,

9
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.970
from gas given off to mass lost.

10
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.510
You'll test the factors
that change the rate,

11
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.740
and picture what the particles
are doing when they collide.

12
00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:36.810
You'll also see how a catalyst
speeds a reaction up without

13
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.510
being used up.

14
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.980
Your mission: find out what
controls the speed of a reaction.
